caneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1369542-contrasting-worldviews-and-views-on-sexuality-in-princess-and-beast?p=1369588#post1369588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What fruit juice are you adding to whiskey?<br /> <br /> More importantly, why didn't that occur to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't go wrong with so co and lemonade. There is also whiskey and orange juice or sour mix. It's called a whiskey sour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T13:12:37-08:00","id":1369628,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve had Jack Daniel\u2019s and lemonade and bourbon mixed with apple juice. Apple juice (with or without whiskey) helps give you lucid dreams. My bff taught my ex that and he taught me. I\u2019ve also had mint juleps on Derby Day and SoCo mixed with cranberry juice (a Scarlett O\u2019Hara) or orange liqueur (a Rhett Butler). Oh, and rum mixed with pineapple juice and vodka mixed with different kinds of fruit juice (pomegranate juice, lemonade and orange juice are all really good).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:50:26-08:00","id":1369681,"title":"","content":"I'm just wondering, is your storyteller incorporating that line of thought into the game you will be playing?I so, may I ask why, what makes beast feeding habits so uniquely horrible that it brought into existence the Radiant Princesses? because if that's how it will be, Heroes would likely have SOME connection to them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T16:24:54-08:00","id":1369690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1369542-contrasting-worldviews-and-views-on-sexuality-in-princess-and-beast?p=1369588#post1369588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What fruit juice are you adding to whiskey?<br /> <br /> More importantly, why didn't that occur to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Citrus juice, normally. Lemon juice of note. Sometimes orange juice. Lime juice potentially, depending on the cocktail recipe.<br /> <br /> Now, there are sour mixes you can buy to make a &quot;whiskey sour&quot;. There are recipes you can find for a whiskey sour as well that use lemon juice and have you need to make a simple syrup (very easy to do).<br /> <br /> If you wanna get CRAZY with it, a traditional whiskey sour uses whiskey (2 ounces, bourbon or rye depending on your preferences), about an ounce of lemon juice, and maybe half an ounce of simple syrup (depends on how heavy you make your simple syrup (like 1 cup sugar to 1 cup or water or 2 cups sugar to 1 cup of water) and how sweet you like your drinks), and..... one egg white. You need to dry shake (no ice) the egg white (either with the other ingredients or not, your choice) in order to break up the protein of the egg white. Then shake it again with ice.<br /> <br /> For some comparison, a real daiquiri is basically 2 ounces rum, 1 ounce lime juice, 1 ounce simple syrup, shaken with ice. And is absolutely delicious. You can basically play around with these ratios for your taste and with the ingredients for different flavors or different alcohols to find your preference.<br /> <br /> &quot;How To Drink&quot; is a really good YouTube channel....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 02-22-2020, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:41:42-08:00","id":1369708,"title":"","content":"Not a fruit juice, but I would really recommend mixing arrack/Swedish punsch (not punch) mixer with blended malt whisky and stir until it clears. Start with a 50/50 ratio and adjust according to taste. The sweet spot is when the sweetness and taste of the arrack mixes with the taste of the whisky without overpowering it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-